MPP Bash Shell Scripts
----------------------
Brief user guide
----------------
Updated		02/08/2005
By		G Coombe
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Each script provides the following standard functionality

<script_name> -?	Provides details of all switches that can
			be used with script.

<script_name> -v	Provides version details of the script.

<script_name> -l	Changes default location of the script log
			file.

<script_name> -a	Will not ask if the user wishes to continue
			with a script.

<script_name> -q	Runs script in quiet mode, but will still write
			to the script log file.

<script_name> -d	Alternative QD data directory.

Error Codes
-----------

All scripts return following error codes.

	0	Completed without error
	1	Completed, but a non fatal warning was encountered
	2	Failed with fatal error

Logging
-------

All scripts (except mpp_bash_functions.sh) log to the logs sub-directory,
with log file name <script_name>_YYYYMMDD.log

Log format
----------
All scripts have log entry lines that contain the following prefix for
each line, except for re-directed output.

YYYYMMDD:HH:MM:SS:<script_name>:<hostname>:<user>:-[INFO|WARN|FATAL]:-<Message text>

mpp_bash_functions.sh
---------------------

This is sourced by all scripts and contains global parameters and functions, if
a script cannot located this file it will exit.

Configuration
-------------

MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY		Set this either via .bashrc etc to be the
				location of the QD database directory.
				eg export MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY=/dbfast1/dwh0
				For most scripts, this is the only setting
				that is required to be able to obtain
				QE information from the QD database.

WORKDIR				In each script, except mpp_bash_functions.sh
				this is set to the directory where the scripts
				are located.
				Default value is:
				WORKDIR=/usr/local/mpp/cdb-pgsql/tools/scripts
				If you change the location of these scripts, the
				above variable must be changed in each script.

MPPROOT				This is set in mpp_bash_functions.sh, default value
				is:
				MPPROOT=/usr/local/mpp/cdb-pgsql
				Once again, if you move the scripts, ensure that this
				value is updated to the revised location.

